 ## Inspect, review, apply, verify
 
+Migration 2039 sets per-table vacuum/analyze scale factors to 0.02/0.01 for
+threads, thread counters, posts, search documents, outbox messages, sessions, rate-limit
+buckets and the two read-state tables. Absolute thresholds, cost limits,
+autovacuum memory and worker counts remain inherited from the cluster.
+Existing fillfactors are preserved. This makes maintenance eligible sooner
+on growing tables; actual scheduling still depends on cluster capacity.
+It adds background I/O and should be assessed using dead tuples, recent
+autovacuum/analyze times and storage latency on the deployment host.
+The migration changes table metadata with a 1-second lock timeout, without
+rewriting tables or running VACUUM FULL. Operators with custom scale factors
+should review these table settings when upgrading and reapply their policy
+afterwards if needed. To revert a table to cluster defaults, use
+`ALTER TABLE public.TABLE_NAME RESET (autovacuum_vacuum_scale_factor,
+autovacuum_analyze_scale_factor)`; restore any earlier custom values instead
+when the installation had them.
