+## Running background work on a separate host
+
+Install the same application release and locked Perl dependencies on the
+worker host. Give it the service environment file with the shared database
+endpoint, session/signing configuration and the mail, antivirus and media
+tools its handlers need. With filesystem attachment storage it must also
+reach the same attachment bytes; PostgreSQL-backed storage uses the shared
+database instead. GlifiStore is not required for this deployment.
+
+Run `gpforum-outbox` and the scheduled-jobs timer on that host; a Hypnotoad
+web service is not needed there. After verifying delivery and scheduled
+operations, stop those background services/timers on web-only hosts. Keep
+partition maintenance assigned to a designated operational host too.
+
+Multiple outbox processes use PostgreSQL's `SKIP LOCKED` claims and distinct
+hostname/PID worker identities. Size their total database connections along
+with every web node, and measure queue age, throughput and handler failures
+before adding consumers. Full batches are drained immediately; `--sleep 5`
+is an idle poll interval, not a mandatory delay after every 100 messages.
+Scheduled jobs remain bounded oneshot runs; keep one timer responsible for
+their cadence rather than starting a timer on every web node.
+
